+
+## 8. Replay set — build & ratio check (2026-10-12, round 10)
+
+`bench/build_replay_set.py` rebuilds the host-recorded traffic into two replay
+files (`bench/.replay/m1/agent.jsonl`, `mem.jsonl`, gitignored) and writes the
+committed manifest `bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/replay_manifest.json`. It
+re-uses the recon inputs only (`inventory.json` tap records, the per-step events
+streams, the mem0 SQLite stores, `mem0_extract_src.txt`, `pi_prompt_src.txt`).
+
+**Selection (meets the "prefer file reads/edits/test output" ask).** The script
+scores each `(run, step)` by `step_score`: `len({read,edit,write} & toolNames)*2`
+`+ 3 if any test-output line ("N passed|failed") +` distinct tool names, then
+picks the 3 highest-scoring steps per arm (baseline and mem0) and spreads 5
+agent turns across each, capped at 30 agent / 12 mem requests. All 6 chosen
+steps are long, file-heavy sessions (each carries 5 agent turns; the baseline
+`/1/2` step additionally has large tool outputs — see §8/`chars_by_role`).
+
+**Agent bodies keep reasoning.** Each assistant message with thinking blocks sets
+`reasoning_content = "\n".join(thinking texts)` under the block's own
+`thinkingSignature` (observed as `'reasoning_content'` in `event_samples.json:457`),
+mirroring pi-ai's openai-completions converter. Dropping it (the pre-round-10
+state) shrank the median from **0.833 → 0.457**, confirming the recorded prompts
+contained the prior reasoning and that it must be replayed for size fidelity. The
+probe server therefore needs `--jinja` (production has it) so the chat template
+renders `reasoning_content`; this is recorded as `server_requirement` in the
+manifest.
+
+**Ratio check (chars/4 estimator vs recorded `prompt_n + cache_n`).**
+
+| role | requests | distinct steps | median est/recorded | in 0.75–1.33 |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|:---:|
+| agent | 30 | 6 (3/ arm) | **0.833** | yes |
+| mem | 12 | 5 | **1.027** | yes |
+
+- `n_messages` mismatches between the rebuilt history length and the recorded
+  `n_messages`: **0** (both roles).
+- Every request carries `recorded_prompt_tokens` (yes, verified in the manifest).
+- The agent 'all-reasoning' and 'reasoning-after-last-user-only' ratios are equal
+  (0.833); expected, because every step is a fresh session with a single user
+  message before all assistant turns — **not** template evidence (see round-10
+  advisory note 1).
+
+**Outliers (est/recorded outside 0.75–1.33): 3 agent, 0 mem.** All three agent
+outliers are `inventory-baseline-r0/0` turns 5, 8 and 10 (ratios **0.740 / 0.743 /
+0.742**, just under the floor):
+
+| id | ratio | reasoning chars | assistant | tool | recorded tokens |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/5 | 0.740 | 25,717 | 4,475 | 2,154 | 13,032 |
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/8 | 0.743 | 26,225 | 5,507 | 3,444 | 13,896 |
+| inventory-baseline-r0/0/10 | 0.742 | 26,591 | 5,918 | 3,753 | 13,815 |
+
+These are the long-reasoning turns of `baseline-r0/0`: the prompt is dominated by
+`reasoning` (≈25–27k chars, ~68% of the total) plus `assistant` and `tool` text.  
+The `chars/4` heuristic under-counts token count when the text tokenizes **denser
+than 4 chars/token**, which is exactly what Qwen-style reasoning and tool/JSON output
+do (short tokens for code, identifiers, paths, numbers, punctuation). Recorded
+tokens (≈13k) therefore exceed `chars/4` (≈9.6k), giving a ratio just below 0.75.
+This is the **expected** below-1 direction for tool-output/JSON/reasoning-heavy
+turns (per the round-8 advisory), not a reconstruction error. It also shows the
+estimator is conservative: dropping reasoning (the pre-round-10 bodies) would put
+these same three at 0.246 / 0.272 / 0.278 — far worse — so the retained
+reasoning is what keeps the whole set in range. No mem outlier; mem ratios all
+1.02–1.04.
+
+**Mem bodies.** System = `ADDITIVE_EXTRACTION_PROMPT` (unescaped, `mem0_extract_src.txt`):
+existing memories = latest-10 live `memory_history` rows (`ADD`/`UPDATE` only, `DELETE`
+dropped) with `created_at` < the **per-call** cutoff (not the 10 nearest by
+embedding); `last_k` from the `messages` table under the same cutoff; `newMessages`=
+`role: content` lines (mem0_extract_src.txt:838); `response_format={type:json_object}`
+and `chat_template_kwargs={enable_thinking:false}` included per mem0. Each of the 12
+requests is tied to one mem tap record (7 `tool_add` / 5 `capture`, kind in the
+manifest), matched to the step's mem events in cutoff order, so every mem replay
+carries its own new-message content and cutoff. `predicted_n==2048` (mem0-r0/2/0
+and mem0-r0/2) is a `max_tokens` cap, noted via `cap_hit_2048`.
+
+**Status for M1.** Replay set is built, committed, and within the ratio bounds
+(§8); ready for the :8089 n-gram probe (spec off vs ≥2 n-gram settings, 1 and 2
+slots busy). The probe must run with `--jinja` (agent bodies) and with mem bodies
+as-is (`enable_thinking:false`, `json_object`), since the spec-on/off comparison must
+share the exact prompt bytes.
+
+**Open / caveat.** The `pi-ai openai-completions.js` source-grep diagnostic returned
+empty in round 10 (the hardcoded node_modules path did not match on the host run);
+the reasoning-content decision is nonetheless validated by the data (0.833 with
+reasoning vs 0.457 without) and by the recorded `thinkingSignature='reasoning_content'`. The builder re-globs the source each run and prints hits, so a future run on the host can confirm the converter line-by-line.
